/// <summary>
/// Stage 5 of 6: work that happens whether or not there is capital budget for it.
///
/// <para>Routine maintenance is applied <b>after</b> the optimiser has run and does not compete
/// for capital budget. It is the pothole filling, the crack sealing, the make-safe work that a
/// network does regardless - and modelling it matters because it is usually the largest single
/// consequence of deferring renewal. A model that leaves it out makes doing nothing look free.</para>
///
/// <para>Return <c>null</c> when none is due. Most elements, most periods, will be null.</para>
///
/// <para><b>The quantity is often not the element's size.</b> Maintenance effort tends to scale
/// with how bad the element is rather than how big it is, so the quantity here is frequently a
/// condition-derived measure. Whatever you choose, be sure it is in the unit the rate in
/// <c>lookups.xlsx</c> is priced in - the two are multiplied and nothing checks that they
/// agree.</para>
///
/// <para><b>Its budget category still has to exist.</b> Maintenance is charged like any other
/// treatment, so its <c>budget_category</c> in the bundle needs a matching column in the client's
/// <c>inputs\budgets.xlsx</c>. The framework checks that at setup and names any mismatch, so this
/// one fails early and clearly rather than quietly.</para>
///
/// <para><b>Set <c>RankParamSimple</c> on whatever you return.</b> Maintenance is not optimised:
/// the framework sorts every maintenance job by that value, descending, and funds down the list
/// until the maintenance budget runs out. Left at its default of zero every job compares equal, so
/// the order is whatever the element loop happened to produce - reproducibly arbitrary, which is
/// worse than randomly arbitrary because it looks deliberate. See
/// <c>docs\patterns\treatment-suitability-scoring.md</c>.</para>
///
/// <para>Static rather than an instance class, because unlike the other stages it needs nothing
/// cached at setup. The canonical models split on this: one keeps a stateful maintenance model
/// built in <c>SetupInstance</c>. Move it to an instance class the moment it needs one.</para>
/// </summary>
public static class RoutineMaintenance
{
